From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer patch: the guest's auxv has AT_PLATFORM "aarch64"

The auxv InitKernelArgs gives the guest linker had no AT_PLATFORM: getauxval(AT_PLATFORM) answered null, where Android's kernel gives "aarch64"
(docs/runtime-identity-matrix.md, process attributes). The string is copied onto the guest stack, as the kernel does, and /proc/self/auxv
(0005) serves the same entry. AT_HWCAP2 stays absent (reads 0), deliberately: of the arm64 HWCAP2 features berberis translates RNDR and I8MM
instructions, but its ID registers (interpreter.h kIdAa64Isar0/1El1) and the cpuinfo Features line (0010) report them absent, and HWCAP2
must agree with both. Module libberberis_arm64.

diff --git a/guest_loader/arm64/guest_loader_arch.cc b/guest_loader/arm64/guest_loader_arch.cc
--- a/guest_loader/arm64/guest_loader_arch.cc
+++ b/guest_loader/arm64/guest_loader_arch.cc
@@ -70,6 +70,12 @@
   // init_progname; the riscv64 path also doesn't set it, but providing the
   // executable path here matches what the kernel would set on a real exec().
   const char* execfn = (argc > 0 && argv[0] != nullptr) ? argv[0] : "<guest>";
+  // apklayer patch (0031): AT_PLATFORM "aarch64" on the guest stack, as the kernel gives it (getauxval(AT_PLATFORM) is null on a stock Berberis).
+  // AT_HWCAP2 stays absent (reads 0): the ID registers and /proc/cpuinfo report the HWCAP2 features berberis can translate (RNDR, I8MM) as absent.
+  static constexpr char kPlatform[] = "aarch64";
+  guest_sp -= sizeof(kPlatform);
+  memcpy(ToHostAddr<char>(guest_sp), kPlatform, sizeof(kPlatform));
+  const GuestAddr platform = guest_sp;
   const uint64_t auxv[] = {
       AT_HWCAP,      kArm64ValueHwcap,
       AT_RANDOM,     ToGuestAddr(random_bytes),
@@ -86,6 +92,7 @@
       AT_GID,        getgid(),
       AT_EGID,       getegid(),
       AT_EXECFN,     reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(execfn),
+      AT_PLATFORM,   platform,
       AT_NULL,
   };

